# GitHub Actions — PR cadence

GitHub Free public repos cap concurrent jobs at 20. Verify uses two jobs and e2e takes ~20–25 min. **Ready** PRs consume that pool; **drafts** do not (`.github/workflows/verify.yml` skips draft jobs).

## Stay draft until local verify

- Open PRs as draft. Keep them draft through intermediate commits.
- Local `pnpm verify` is the inner gate. Do not poll Actions after every push.

## Mark ready once

- Mark ready only after local `pnpm verify` passes and the PR is the merge candidate.
- Do not mark ready on the first push, then keep pushing. Each later synchronize cancels in-progress Verify and starts a new e2e.

```text
# ❌ BAD — ready immediately, five more pushes, wait on Actions while still editing
# ✅ GOOD — draft until pnpm verify is green, mark ready once, merge when CI is green
```

## At most ~8 non-draft PRs

Before marking ready, count open non-draft PRs targeting `main`. If there are already about eight, **stay draft**. Do not mark ready to “get in the queue.”

Many agents may code in parallel. Only a handful should be ready and waiting on Verify. Merge when green so slots free.

Do not use larger GitHub runners to raise the cap. See [github-actions-standard-runners.mdc](github-actions-standard-runners.mdc).
